issue.body:
I recently switched from browserify to webpack and am now using your great plugin `broccoli-webpack-cached`. Thanks for creating this :)

I am having one issue and that is webpack is rebuilding on _all_ changes, even ones outside its domain. I am currently only using webpack to bundle js, not css, and with my previous `Brocfile`, browserify would not run on a css change. However, now webpack is running on all changes even css files. With browserify, I was able to prevent this behavior like this:

```
let js = new Funnel(js, {
  include: [/.js$/, /.jsx$/],
});

// Now pass the js tree to webpack or browserify
```

Do you have any suggestions on how to prevent rebuilds when changing a file that is not javascript? Thanks!
